way, you're not going

00:24:30.540 --> 00:24:31.960
to get anything that's designed

00:24:31.960 --> 00:24:33.580
to be this

00:24:33.580 --> 00:24:34.420
puzzle-solving

00:24:34.420 --> 00:24:36.560
tool, but you can

00:24:36.560 --> 00:24:37.520
still get

00:24:37.520 --> 00:24:38.860
creative with these things,

00:24:38.920 --> 00:24:40.200
which I think is more important

00:24:40.200 --> 00:24:41.720
than sort of

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:45.000
a hand-crafted

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.320
puzzle. What it came

00:24:46.320 --> 00:24:47.280
down to for me too,

00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:48.820
is this doesn't

00:24:48.820 --> 00:24:49.660
have to be a

00:24:49.660 --> 00:24:51.140
puzzle game in that respect

00:24:51.140 --> 00:24:53.440
where you're

00:24:53.440 --> 00:24:54.800
actually having to think about where

00:24:54.800 --> 00:24:56.360
you place your bombs in order

00:24:56.360 --> 00:24:57.400
to trap enemies,

00:24:57.420 --> 00:24:59.100
it didn't have to be that kind of

00:24:59.100 --> 00:25:00.820
level of game, like it is just

00:25:00.820 --> 00:25:01.880
supposed to be a game where you

00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:03.200
blow stuff up and have fun

00:25:03.200 --> 00:25:05.400
doing that, so I respect that

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:06.520
they didn't go puzzle route,

00:25:06.700 --> 00:25:08.000
but I think the

00:25:08.000 --> 00:25:08.980
worst game design

00:25:08.980 --> 00:25:09.900
decision they had

00:25:09.900 --> 00:25:11.540
was that enemies

00:25:11.540 --> 00:25:12.780
don't necessarily

00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:14.320
have patterns,

00:25:14.320 --> 00:25:15.460
and I understand

00:25:15.460 --> 00:25:17.500
that certain enemies

00:25:17.500 --> 00:25:18.420
are a little tougher

00:25:18.420 --> 00:25:19.400
than others,

00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:20.700
and certain enemies

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:21.720
behave differently

00:25:21.720 --> 00:25:23.940
than others, but there needed to

00:25:23.940 --> 00:25:25.260
be something where

00:25:25.260 --> 00:25:26.620
like, for instance,

00:25:26.760 --> 00:25:27.900
those balloon enemies, right,

00:25:27.960 --> 00:25:29.200
I think they're the first ones you see

00:25:29.200 --> 00:25:31.280
in the whole game, they needed to just

00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:32.300
be an enemy that

00:25:32.300 --> 00:25:33.880
goes side to side,

00:25:34.340 --> 00:25:35.940
you know, left to right,

00:25:36.140 --> 00:25:37.400
and you learn based

00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:38.360
off of that, that like,

00:25:38.660 --> 00:25:40.440
okay, I don't want to go in their hole

00:25:40.440 --> 00:25:41.260
because then I'll

00:25:41.260 --> 00:25:42.560
just get caught in their corner,

00:25:43.080 --> 00:25:44.400
but I can bomb

00:25:44.400 --> 00:25:45.460
them, and I can time

00:25:45.460 --> 00:25:46.320
my bomb based

00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:47.860
on like, them coming in

00:25:47.860 --> 00:25:48.940
this particular direction,

00:25:49.940 --> 00:25:51.480
instead, the game handles

00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:53.160
everybody as a

00:25:53.160 --> 00:25:54.580
free-thinking,

00:25:54.860 --> 00:25:55.660
but without thought

00:25:55.660 --> 00:25:57.620
really, roaming character

00:25:57.620 --> 00:25:58.680
that doesn't,

00:25:59.060 --> 00:26:00.220
like, sometimes it feels

00:26:00.220 --> 00:26:01.180
like they know about your bombs,

00:26:01.400 --> 00:26:02.640
sometimes it feels like they know

00:26:02.640 --> 00:26:04.080
where you are, but as far as

00:26:04.080 --> 00:26:05.400
I'm concerned, the whole thing

00:26:05.400 --> 00:26:07.200
in terms of enemies is just completely

00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:08.580
random, and more often

00:26:08.580 --> 00:26:10.040
than not, they can just

00:26:10.040 --> 00:26:10.880
run into your

00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:11.740
explosions by

00:26:11.740 --> 00:26:14.300
accident, they are actually

00:26:14.300 --> 00:26:15.580
always walking

00:26:15.580 --> 00:26:16.680
in the direction of your bombs

00:26:16.680 --> 00:26:17.560
if you're placing them smart,

00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:19.320
they don't know where these bombs

00:26:19.320 --> 00:26:20.580
are in relation to you,

00:26:20.880 --> 00:26:22.080
and I think

00:26:22.080 --> 00:26:23.340
patterns would have helped something

00:26:23.340 --> 00:26:24.880
like that if you had guys who

00:26:24.880 --> 00:26:26.140
went in circles

00:26:26.140 --> 00:26:27.200
and got, and like,

00:26:27.280 --> 00:26:28.400
later on with the ghosts,

00:26:28.560 --> 00:26:30.480
like, if they had like,

00:26:31.000 --> 00:26:32.460
you know, because they can go through the

00:26:32.460 --> 00:26:34.020
different blocks, if they had a

00:26:34.020 --> 00:26:35.180
recognizable pattern

00:26:35.180 --> 00:26:36.060
so that you

00:26:36.060 --> 00:26:37.160
could think about where you're

00:26:37.160 --> 00:26:38.140
going to place your bombs,

00:26:38.220 --> 00:26:39.480
rather than just

00:26:40.100 --> 00:26:41.680
being in this awkward situation

00:26:41.680 --> 00:26:42.900
later on, when there's only

00:26:42.900 --> 00:26:43.980
like a few enemies left,

00:26:44.180 --> 00:26:45.100
where you're kind of like chasing

00:26:45.100 --> 00:26:46.140
them around the screen,

00:26:46.340 --> 00:26:47.260
and only ever

00:26:47.260 --> 00:26:49.080
like, getting kind of

00:26:49.080 --> 00:26:49.960
like, okay, well I'm going to

00:26:49.960 --> 00:26:50.780
place one here,

00:26:50.840 --> 00:26:52.280
and I have another one, so I'll place this

00:26:52.280 --> 00:26:53.700
here, and then I trap them,

00:26:53.880 --> 00:26:54.720
and that's great,

00:26:54.900 --> 00:26:57.140
but there's also times where trapping

00:26:57.140 --> 00:26:58.200
them isn't an option because you've

00:26:58.200 --> 00:26:59.020
destroyed every

00:26:59.020 --> 00:27:00.120
single block, and now they're

00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:01.020
just roaming around

00:27:01.020 --> 00:27:02.180
this stage randomly,

00:27:02.380 --> 00:27:03.300
and you just kind of have to

00:27:03.300 --> 00:27:04.320
hope that one

00:27:04.320 --> 00:27:05.640
of your explosions is lucky enough

00:27:05.640 --> 00:27:06.920
to hit them. They introduce

00:27:06.920 --> 00:27:07.840
such a wide

00:27:07.840 --> 00:27:08.740
variety of

00:27:08.740 --> 00:27:10.940
enemies aesthetically,

00:27:11.560 --> 00:27:12.700
but for the most part,

00:27:12.800 --> 00:27:13.620
like most of them all do

00:27:13.620 --> 00:27:16.120
the same thing, so it tricks you

00:27:16.120 --> 00:27:17.100
into thinking like, oh, there's an

00:27:17.600 --> 00:27:18.660
enemy variety, but they're

00:27:18.660 --> 00:27:19.800
all kind of the same.

00:27:19.900 --> 00:27:21.200
Well, I'd say that,

00:27:21.260 --> 00:27:22.480
yeah, they definitely

00:27:22.480 --> 00:27:23.380
don't have

00:27:23.380 --> 00:27:24.840
patterns, but I think

00:27:24.840 --> 00:27:25.980
that they do have tendencies.

00:27:26.320 --> 00:27:28.860
Like, I remember the barrels,

00:27:28.960 --> 00:27:30.120
they move a

00:27:30.120 --> 00:27:31.760
little bit faster, but they stick

00:27:31.760 --> 00:27:32.600
to a left-right

00:27:32.600 --> 00:27:34.220
thing, or an up-down

00:27:34.220 --> 00:27:35.220
thing, depending on

00:27:35.220 --> 00:27:36.080
where,

00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:38.240
like, whatever their

00:27:38.240 --> 00:27:39.420
initial state was.

00:27:39.540 --> 00:27:40.620
Like, they are much

00:27:40.620 --> 00:27:41.460
less likely

00:27:41.460 --> 00:27:43.040
to veer off

00:27:43.040 --> 00:27:45.100
of a one-axis

00:27:45.100 --> 00:27:46.440
path, but I think

00:27:46.440 --> 00:27:47.440
that's okay. I mean,

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:48.520
I think that

00:27:48.520 --> 00:27:50.060
if you just

00:27:50.060 --> 00:27:51.940
have this grid,

00:27:51.940 --> 00:27:53.120
and all the

00:27:53.120 --> 00:27:54.520
enemies have

00:27:54.520 --> 00:27:55.800
very predictable

00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:57.000
behaviors, you're just

00:27:57.000 --> 00:27:57.940
sort of optimizing,

00:27:57.960 --> 00:28:02.420
like, your playthrough

00:28:02.420 --> 00:28:03.280
will be, like,

00:28:03.560 --> 00:28:04.560
how optimally

00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:05.440
can I do this,

00:28:05.460 --> 00:28:08.560
instead of, like, how can I,

00:28:09.420 --> 00:28:10.320
like, sort of

00:28:10.320 --> 00:28:11.360
crowd control this,

00:28:11.600 --> 00:28:12.400
which is

00:28:12.400 --> 00:28:14.100
also a

00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:16.200
valid way to play the

00:28:16.200 --> 00:28:17.320
game, or to design

00:28:17.320 --> 00:28:18.660
the game. So I don't

00:28:18.660 --> 00:28:20.060
think it needed to be this

00:28:20.060 --> 00:28:21.100
cut-and-dry

00:28:21.100 --> 00:28:23.620
pattern thing. Yeah,

00:28:23.700 --> 00:28:24.540
I guess now that I'm looking at it,

00:28:24.540 --> 00:28:25.460
I'm actually watching right now,

00:28:25.620 --> 00:28:26.860
yeah, there are some that go

00:28:26.860 --> 00:28:27.700
left and right,

00:28:28.900 --> 00:28:29.860
yeah, that just wasn't as

00:28:29.860 --> 00:28:31.820
noticeable to me. I still agree

00:28:31.820 --> 00:28:33.620
with Mike, though. I feel like

00:28:33.620 --> 00:28:35.700
having a lot

00:28:35.700 --> 00:28:37.360
more specific patterns would

00:28:37.360 --> 00:28:38.760
have helped

00:28:38.760 --> 00:28:41.120
this game just help

00:28:41.120 --> 00:28:42.260
the levels feel,

00:28:43.780 --> 00:28:44.960
I don't know, like,

00:28:45.040 --> 00:28:47.500
a little bit more, it would help

00:28:47.500 --> 00:28:49.940
the levels. They would have

00:28:49.940 --> 00:28:51.180
been tighter because you would

00:28:51.180 --> 00:28:53.280
have had, you would have

00:28:53.280 --> 00:28:54.160
had a path

00:28:54.160 --> 00:28:55.080
in mind. Yeah,

00:28:55.160 --> 00:28:56.340
that's it, you have a plan

00:28:56.340 --> 00:28:58.180
of action. Right,

00:28:58.280 --> 00:28:59.380
I'm not arguing that

00:28:59.380 --> 00:29:00.500
they should all act

00:29:00.500 --> 00:29:01.400
like Koopa Troopas,

00:29:01.480 --> 00:29:02.900
right? That would

00:29:02.900 --> 00:29:03.800
be a really boring Super

00:29:03.800 --> 00:29:04.860
Mario Bros. game if you

00:29:04.860 --> 00:29:05.840
ever only went up against

00:29:05.840 --> 00:29:08.020
Koopa Troopas, but every

00:29:08.020 --> 00:29:09.020
enemy in a

00:29:09.020 --> 00:29:10.380
Mario Bros. game is

00:29:11.360 --> 00:29:12.320
somewhat designed

00:29:12.320 --> 00:29:13.900
to do a particular pattern.

00:29:14.240 --> 00:29:15.480
I think the

00:29:15.480 --> 00:29:16.460
Hammer Bros. are a good

00:29:16.460 --> 00:29:17.640
example of something where

00:29:17.640 --> 00:29:18.900
it feels really random

00:29:18.900 --> 00:29:19.760
and you kind

00:29:19.760 --> 00:29:20.660
of have to think about when are

00:29:20.660 --> 00:29:21.520
they going to jump, when are

00:29:21.520 --> 00:29:22.660
they going to throw hammers, when are

00:29:22.660 --> 00:29:23.880
they going to do these things? I guess

00:29:23.880 --> 00:29:25.220
I'm showing how bad

00:29:25.220 --> 00:29:26.420
of a game designer I

00:29:26.420 --> 00:29:27.520
would be if the only thing

00:29:27.520 --> 00:29:28.700
I can think about is

00:29:29.500 --> 00:29:31.000
movement patterns, but I'm sure

00:29:31.000 --> 00:29:32.120
there's other things they could

00:29:32.120 --> 00:29:33.340
have done, too, for these

00:29:33.340 --> 00:29:34.360
enemies to

00:29:34.360 --> 00:29:35.520
differentiate them on a

00:29:35.520 --> 00:29:38.820
level that would make

00:29:38.820 --> 00:29:40.160
them more interesting than

00:29:40.160 --> 00:29:41.560
just these

00:29:41.560 --> 00:29:42.380
guys float

00:29:42.380 --> 00:29:43.740
around the screen and you

00:29:43.740 --> 00:29:44.700
just have to make sure you

00:29:44.700 --> 00:29:45.620
bomb them. Well,

00:29:45.720 --> 00:29:46.700
so for example,

00:29:47.240 --> 00:29:48.580
when I first saw the barrel

00:29:48.580 --> 00:29:50.720
enemies, my first

00:29:50.720 --> 00:29:52.060
thought was, oh, that must be

00:29:52.060 --> 00:29:53.240
like a barrel of gunpowder

00:29:53.240 --> 00:29:54.580
or something, and when I place a bomb,

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:56.260
they're going to blow up

00:29:56.260 --> 00:29:57.340
my bomb immediately or

00:29:57.340 --> 00:29:58.600
something. This is

00:29:58.600 --> 00:29:59.580
something else I would have to think

00:29:59.580 --> 00:30:00.460
about, like, okay, don't place

00:30:00.460 --> 00:30:01.380
a bomb too close to the

00:30:01.380 --> 00:30:02.520
barrel guy because he'll

00:30:02.520 --> 00:30:03.620
blow up all my bombs or

00:30:03.620 --> 00:30:04.760
something. I don't know, it doesn't

00:30:04.760 --> 00:30:05.860
really make sense when I think about it,

00:30:05.860 --> 00:30:07.200
but that kind of

00:30:09.100 --> 00:30:10.080
thing that I would have to think

00:30:10.080 --> 00:30:12.220
about would make the

00:30:12.220 --> 00:30:14.460
game feel take longer

00:30:14.460 --> 00:30:15.720
to get stale. Yeah,

00:30:15.720 --> 00:30:16.560
I get

00:30:16.560 --> 00:30:18.520
what you're saying, like, that is

00:30:18.520 --> 00:30:19.600
another element

00:30:21.380 --> 00:30:22.260
that, like,

00:30:22.400 --> 00:30:23.420
if maybe

00:30:23.420 --> 00:30:24.520
it just, like, actually just

00:30:24.520 --> 00:30:25.860
made your explosion bigger and

00:30:25.860 --> 00:30:27.340
then that way it could reach

00:30:27.340 --> 00:30:28.240
you accidentally.

00:30:28.560 --> 00:30:29.480
I get that.

00:30:30.040 --> 00:30:31.200
Right. I sort of

00:30:31.200 --> 00:30:32.940
had that intuition as

00:30:32.940 --> 00:30:34.600
well. Yeah,

00:30:34.700 --> 00:30:35.600
rather than, like, right now,

00:30:35.740 --> 00:30:37.360
it's still just, granted,

00:30:37.360 --> 00:30:38.240
there might be, like, little different

00:30:38.240 --> 00:30:39.180
ways of figuring out

00:30:39.180 --> 00:30:40.180
how to get people, like,

00:30:40.240 --> 00:30:41.100
how to get each enemy

00:30:41.100 --> 00:30:42.500
depending on which direction

00:30:42.500 --> 00:30:43.900
they're moving, but it's

00:30:43.900 --> 00:30:45.960
still always just bomb

00:30:45.960 --> 00:30:47.040
all the enemies. Like,

00:30:47.120 --> 00:30:48.040
I know that's the name of the game,

00:30:48.140 --> 00:30:50.380
but, like, I feel like, I don't know,

00:30:50.400 --> 00:30:51.320
there could be another level.

00:30:51.680 --> 00:30:52.680
I've got one more,

00:30:54.100 --> 00:30:55.060
one more example of

00:30:55.060 --> 00:30:56.640
something I was thinking

00:30:56.640 --> 00:30:57.500
of. It might kind of go back

00:30:57.500 --> 00:30:58.380
to what we were talking about before

00:30:58.380 --> 00:30:59.500
with the power-ups, but,

00:30:59.900 --> 00:31:00.720
Sean, you mentioned

00:31:00.720 --> 00:31:01.800
you were

00:31:01.800 --> 00:31:02.860
doing something that was,

00:31:03.380 --> 00:31:04.260
you were almost like creating

00:31:04.260 --> 00:31:05.640
a little bit of a puzzle for yourself

00:31:06.080 --> 00:31:07.180
that wasn't, like, in the game

00:31:07.180 --> 00:31:08.180
design, and I was kind of doing

00:31:08.180 --> 00:31:09.400
something similar where when I

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:10.560
had a very

00:31:10.560 --> 00:31:11.540
large blast radius,

00:31:11.960 --> 00:31:13.020
I would try and put

00:31:13.020 --> 00:31:13.980
bombs at

00:31:13.980 --> 00:31:15.200
the edge of another

00:31:15.200 --> 00:31:17.000
bomb's blast radius in a

00:31:17.000 --> 00:31:19.520
way where I could fill the

00:31:19.520 --> 00:31:20.500
whole board as much as I

00:31:20.500 --> 00:31:21.700
can, get as many enemies across

00:31:21.700 --> 00:31:23.580
the whole board with one explosion

00:31:23.580 --> 00:31:24.500
without having to detonate

00:31:24.500 --> 00:31:25.940
more than once. It didn't

00:31:25.940 --> 00:31:26.840
really make a difference,

00:31:26.900 --> 00:31:27.880
because if I

00:31:27.880 --> 00:31:28.760
didn't have them like that,

00:31:28.780 --> 00:31:30.020
I could have just detonated them all one

00:31:30.020 --> 00:31:31.440
after another and still gotten that

00:31:31.440 --> 00:31:32.720
same range, but it was

00:31:32.720 --> 00:31:33.920
just fun to me to do it that way,

00:31:33.960 --> 00:31:34.960
and I kind of wished

00:31:34.960 --> 00:31:35.800
that the game

00:31:35.800 --> 00:31:36.900
would have rewarded me

00:31:36.900 --> 00:31:37.840
for some way

00:31:37.840 --> 00:31:40.720
in doing that. points stack

00:31:40.720 --> 00:31:41.780
on each other, or just some

00:31:41.780 --> 00:31:43.120
incentive to do something

00:31:43.120 --> 00:31:44.260
different than just place

00:31:44.260 --> 00:31:45.100
bombs and blow them

00:31:45.100 --> 00:31:46.100
up until

00:31:46.100 --> 00:31:48.340
you kill everything. I guess.

00:31:48.540 --> 00:31:49.800
I mean, also,

00:31:50.040 --> 00:31:51.500
if you frame it not so

00:31:51.500 --> 00:31:52.700
much as solving a

00:31:52.700 --> 00:31:53.700
puzzle or

00:31:53.700 --> 00:31:54.680
solving something

00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:55.860
that the game is laying out

00:31:55.860 --> 00:31:58.060
in front of you, but a more

00:31:58.060 --> 00:31:58.920
proactive way

00:31:58.920 --> 00:31:59.860
of thinking of like, oh,

00:31:59.880 --> 00:32:01.020
I'm laying a trap,

00:32:02.140 --> 00:32:03.620
that's sort of how I

00:32:03.620 --> 00:32:04.500
was looking at it,

00:32:05.360 --> 00:32:06.320
and I

00:32:06.320 --> 00:32:08.580
think that was sort

00:32:08.580 --> 00:32:09.380
of my

00:32:10.060 --> 00:32:11.020
reward was

00:32:11.020 --> 00:32:12.100
knowing that I laid

00:32:12.100 --> 00:32:12.980
this successful

00:32:12.980 --> 00:32:14.240
trap. I know that

00:32:14.240 --> 00:32:15.240
that's like

